\section{Modes}{

\itemize{
\item \strong{regression}: PLS regression of a single numeric outcome.
\item \strong{classification}: PLS discriminant analysis (PLS-DA). The factor outcome
is coded as one dummy column per class and regressed on the predictors
with a single multi-response PLS model (PLS2). Classes and class
probabilities depend on the engine argument \code{prob_method}:
\itemize{
\item \code{"lda"} (default): linear discriminant analysis (\code{\link[MASS:lda]{MASS::lda()}}, priors =
training class proportions) on the first \code{num_comp} PLS scores. Gives
proper posterior probabilities; the predicted class is the most
probable one.
\item \code{"softmax"}: softmax of the predicted dummy values; the predicted class
is the class with the largest predicted dummy (classic PLS-DA "max"
rule). The probabilities rank observations correctly (ROC AUC is fine)
but are not calibrated.
}
}
