\section{Tuning parameters}{

\itemize{
\item \code{num_comp} (\pkg{dials} \code{\link[dials:num_comp]{dials::num_comp()}}; default range 1--4, so pass
e.g. \code{num_comp(range = c(1, 15))} to the grid) is mapped to \code{ncomp}.
It is clamped to \code{min(num_comp, n - 1, p)}, so that small resamples do
not break a grid. When missing, \code{min(10, n - 1, p)} components are used.
}

\code{num_comp} is a \emph{submodel} parameter: one fit with the largest value serves
all smaller values through \code{\link[parsnip:multi_predict]{parsnip::multi_predict()}}, so tuning
\code{num_comp} costs a single fit per resample.

\code{predictor_prop} (sparse PLS) is not supported by this engine: setting it
raises an error. Use the \code{"mixOmics"} engine for sparse PLS.
